---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout title="About | Ride The Tide Research" description="South Africa's peptide research community. Evidence-based protocols, safety-first education, and practical guides for researchers.">
  <div class="mx-auto max-w-4xl px-4 py-12 lg:px-8">
    <h1 class="text-3xl font-bold text-slate-900 mb-8">About Ride The Tide Research</h1>
    
    <div class="prose max-w-none">
      <p class="text-lg text-slate-600 mb-6">
        Ride The Tide Research is South Africa's dedicated resource for peptide research information. 
        We combine clinical evidence with practical protocols to help researchers make informed, safe decisions.
      </p>

      <h2>Our Mission</h2>
      <p>
        The peptide research space is flooded with bro-science, miracle claims, and unverified information. 
        Most resources are US or EU-centric, with little consideration for South African regulations, 
        suppliers, and context.
      </p>
      <p>
        We're changing that. Every article is grounded in primary research, written with a safety-first mindset, 
        and contextualized for the South African research community.
      </p>

      <h2>What We Do</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Peptide Deep Dives</strong> — Mechanism, dosing, cycling, and stacking for 98+ compounds</li>
        <li><strong>Protocol Guides</strong> — Step-by-step guides for reconstitution, injection, storage, and bloodwork</li>
        <li><strong>South African Context</strong> — Local laws, suppliers, shipping, and regulatory guidance</li>
        <li><strong>Safety & Science</strong> — Side effects, interactions, contraindications, and medical oversight</li>
        <li><strong>Case Studies</strong> — Real results, protocol breakdowns, and transformation stories</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Our Approach</h2>
      <p>
        <strong>Scientific but accessible.</strong> We cite primary research, explain mechanisms simply, 
        and never dumb it down or hype it up.
      </p>
      <p>
        <strong>Safety-obsessed.</strong> Every article leads with risks, contraindications, and the need 
        for medical supervision. We believe informed researchers are safe researchers.
      </p>
      <p>
        <strong>South African context.</strong> We reference SAHPRA regulations, local suppliers, 
        Cape Town and Johannesburg shipping considerations, and South African healthcare context.
      </p>

      <h2>Medical Disclaimer</h2>
      <div class="disclaimer-box">
        <p>
          <strong>All content on this site is for research and educational purposes only.</strong> 
          Peptide compounds are not approved for human use by SAHPRA or the FDA. 
          Always consult a qualified healthcare professional before using any peptide. 
          Individual results may vary. We do not provide medical advice, diagnosis, or treatment.
        </p>
      </div>

      <h2>Contact</h2>
      <p>
        <strong>Research inquiries:</strong> <a href="mailto:research@ridethetide.site">research@ridethetide.site</a><br>
        <strong>Protocol coaching:</strong> <a href="https://ridethetide.site/quiz">ridethetide.site/quiz</a><br>
        <strong>Protocol tracker:</strong> <a href="https://www.ridethetide.info/">ridethetide.info</a>
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</Layout>
